Subject: [PATCH] mtk: sugov: select a valid CPU for all-idle policy samples

cpu_id is assigned only when a sampled active ratio is greater than zero.
When all CPUs in a policy are idle, it remains uninitialized and is used
to index last_idle_duratio. Default to the first CPU of the existing
nonempty policy mask, preserving the current strict-greater tie rule.

This prevents an undefined array access in the idle-ramp decision without
changing activity ratios, thresholds, frequency tables or CPU topology.
It targets the Rodin vendor scheduler module, not the common boot image.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/sugov/nonlinear_opp_cap.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/sugov/nonlinear_opp_cap.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/sugov/nonlinear_opp_cap.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/sugov/nonlinear_opp_cap.c
@@ -2481,7 +2481,8 @@
 void update_active_ratio_policy(struct cpumask *cpumask)
 {
-	unsigned int cpu_idx, cpu_id, first_cpu = cpumask_first(cpumask);
+	unsigned int cpu_idx, first_cpu = cpumask_first(cpumask);
+	unsigned int cpu_id = first_cpu;
 	unsigned int policy_max_active_ratio_tmp = 0;
 
 	for_each_cpu(cpu_idx, cpumask) {
 		cpu_active_ratio_cap[cpu_idx] = update_cpu_active_ratio(cpu_idx);
